WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.440
Switzerland, 2024.

2
00:00:01.490 --> 00:00:08.250
UN estimates put international migrants
at 31.1 per cent of the population.

3
00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:10.350
The figure for the whole world that year:

4
00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:12.230
3.7 per cent.

5
00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:17.790
In Switzerland, citizens can force a
national vote on changing the constitution.

6
00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:24.090
On 9 February 2014, an initiative to
limit immigration won 50.3 per cent yes.

7
00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:26.410
A narrow majority.

8
00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:28.470
The vote was accepted.

9
00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:31.730
So what did the Swiss
government actually do next?

10
00:00:31.780 --> 00:00:36.170
In this mission, you'll sort immigration
into documented and undocumented,

11
00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:38.410
and the ways governments respond.

12
00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:43.310
Then you'll measure how Switzerland's
migrant share has changed since 1990.

13
00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:48.270
Your mission: find out what the Swiss
government did after the 2014 vote, and

14
00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:48.930
why.
